This design represents a complete, production-ready, modular Enterprise Identity and Access Management (IAM) Provider built in **C# using ASP.NET Core**. 

The system is decoupled into three primary modules:
1. **User Directory Subsystem**: Manages secure high-entropy PBKDF2-SHA512 hashing, salt generation, and a thread-safe sliding account locking mechanism.
2. **Token Revocation Subsystem**: Tracks blacklisted session tokens using a thread-safe `ConcurrentDictionary` and a background sweeping process (`BackgroundService`) to clear expired records.
3. **OpenID Connect & JWT Subsystem**: Provides asymmetric key management (generating ephemeral RS256 keys), standard OpenID Discovery Metadata (`/.well-known/openid-configuration`), JWKS endpoints (`/.well-known/jwks.json`), and a secure JWT token issuance engine.

---

### Project Architecture & Dependencies

To compile and run this system, ensure your project file (`.csproj`) includes the following packages:

```xml
<ItemGroup>
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer" Version="8.0.0" />
  <PackageReference Include="System.IdentityModel.Tokens.Jwt" Version="7.2.0" />
  <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.IdentityModel.Tokens" Version="7.2.0" />
</ItemGroup>
```

